<title>USA: TABLE - Vencor Inc sells $750 mln 144a notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Vencor Inc sells $750 mln 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Vencor Inc was priced Wednesday via lead manager JP Morgan Securities Inc, according to a market source.</p>
<p>The deal was increased to $750 million from an original size of $500 million, the source added.</p>
<p>Vencor Inc, operates acute care hospitals; nursing centers; pharmacies, and assisted living communities.</p>
<p>BORROWER VENCOR INC</p>
<p>AMT $750 MLN	 COUPON 8.625 PCT  MATURITY 7/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 99.575  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998 LAST MOODY'S B1    YIELD 8.69 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-B  SPREAD +250 BPS   CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
